SUMMARY:Buddhist Ghost Festival (Ullambana)
DESCRIPTION:History: In many East and Southeast Asian Buddhist and folk traditions\, the Ghost Festival (Ullambana\, Zhongyuan) marks a time when offerings are made for ancestors and hungry ghosts.\nTraditions: Families visit temples\, burn incense\, offer food\, and set out lanterns or paper offerings to guide and comfort wandering spirits.\nFeasting: Seasonal plates vary by region\, often including rice\, fruit\, tea\, vegetarian dishes\, and family recipes shared in remembrance.\nDay: Friday\n\nIcon: 🏮\nCategory: cultural
CATEGORIES:cultural
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
