SUMMARY:Rosh Hashanah (Jewish New Year)
DESCRIPTION:History: Rosh Hashanah\, the head of the Hebrew year on 1–2 T
 ishrei\, opens the Ten Days of Awe that end with Yom Kippur\; tradition ho
 lds it as the anniversary of creation and the day of judgement.\nTradition
 s: The shofar is sounded in synagogue\, greetings of shanah tovah are exch
 anged\, and at Tashlich bread crumbs are cast into flowing water to symbol
 ically shed the past year's wrongs.\nFeasting: Apples dipped in honey for 
 a sweet year\, round challah\, pomegranates for a year full of merit\, hon
